WEBVTT

00:03.280 --> 00:06.320
This kid won't be getting up for a while.

00:06.320 --> 00:07.610
Well, then...

00:07.610 --> 00:09.320
I guess I should get to work.

00:15.570 --> 00:17.710
What, are you here for me?

00:18.230 --> 00:19.560
Or...

01:57.200 --> 02:00.390
Are you really going to help me?

02:00.390 --> 02:01.160
Yeah.

02:01.820 --> 02:03.200
Really?

02:03.610 --> 02:04.440
Yeah.

02:10.850 --> 02:12.400
<i>She's all right.</i>

02:16.940 --> 02:18.310
Alcyone...

02:18.950 --> 02:20.440
Lady Philomela...

02:23.970 --> 02:25.200
Lady Philomela.

02:28.450 --> 02:30.020
Why...

02:33.610 --> 02:38.050
Why do you interfere when you know nothing?!

02:38.050 --> 02:39.790
She's the same as Philomela.

02:39.790 --> 02:42.700
Must be the magic book's influence.

02:43.310 --> 02:48.610
She's being dragged in by the thing 
inside that's trying to get out.

02:49.330 --> 02:51.610
How? We broke the circle.

02:52.180 --> 02:54.010
The circle's just an opportunity.

02:54.010 --> 02:55.990
It's merely an aid. It's not that important.

02:56.740 --> 03:01.490
Magic and sorcery is all up to
 the will of the living in the end.

03:01.740 --> 03:04.320
You have no business here!

03:04.320 --> 03:05.990
Why do you involve yourself?

03:06.720 --> 03:14.990
What does it matter to you what happens 
to her, or to me, or to this house?!

03:15.920 --> 03:18.450
Philomela is a good person.

03:18.800 --> 03:22.370
She thanked me when I was being nosy.

03:23.070 --> 03:24.840
She even gave me advice.

03:25.400 --> 03:28.220
There are plenty of people like that.

03:28.220 --> 03:31.610
Hiding, suffering, dying...

03:32.370 --> 03:38.360
But I don't want to pretend I don't see when 
she's right there where I can reach her.

03:38.920 --> 03:43.610
What you're trying to do makes sense to you.

03:44.170 --> 03:46.320
But not to me.

03:47.030 --> 03:50.330
And if Philomela's going to 
be consumed for your sake...

03:51.990 --> 03:53.160
I'll stop you!

03:53.390 --> 03:58.230
You don't even have something 
you'd be willing to pay any price for!

03:58.840 --> 04:00.060
Get back!

04:04.690 --> 04:06.810
He was my only one...

04:06.810 --> 04:12.560
He was my lovely, disgusting, only one...

04:12.960 --> 04:14.700
And he was taken from me!

04:15.180 --> 04:16.910
Taken!

04:20.770 --> 04:24.600
What's taken from me must be taken back!

04:35.350 --> 04:36.240
The werewolf!

04:36.580 --> 04:38.960
You've returned to your senses?!

04:39.380 --> 04:40.700
Wretched witch!

04:40.700 --> 04:43.310
My god has freed me from your shackles!

04:44.060 --> 04:47.170
<i>You're</i> the one that will face
 a trial of lightning and ice!

04:49.290 --> 04:51.650
Your children aren't here.

04:51.650 --> 04:55.150
The only child to be here is mine.

04:55.150 --> 04:59.940
Your children are nowhere in this world.

04:59.940 --> 05:01.330
You lie!

05:01.330 --> 05:04.660
Who would believe what a witch has to say?!

05:04.660 --> 05:06.690
You're hiding...

05:07.220 --> 05:08.970
You're hiding my children!

05:16.140 --> 05:17.880
Pitiful woman...

05:18.310 --> 05:19.800
Forgive me.

05:20.320 --> 05:27.690
I cannot allow you to break <i>it</i>, either.

05:47.300 --> 05:52.420
Alcyone, I'm going to have 
you be Philomela's shield.

05:53.930 --> 05:58.700
When you're destroyed out of malice, 
that will become the trigger.

05:59.750 --> 06:03.050
So please, do all you can to protect her.

06:06.130 --> 06:10.420
<i>So that's the other thing that 
was attached to the core.</i>

06:11.410 --> 06:12.350
You!

06:12.820 --> 06:16.640
"Let's make sure I never see you again."

06:16.640 --> 06:21.560
Or at least, that was his 
wish, but here we are.

06:22.540 --> 06:25.700
You've done your duty, Alcyone.

06:26.380 --> 06:27.890
It must have been difficult.

06:29.630 --> 06:30.680
No...

06:31.210 --> 06:33.880
No, Master.

06:33.880 --> 06:37.510
This was my duty.

06:37.510 --> 06:40.790
Then it's time I carry out my duty, too.

06:47.070 --> 06:48.630
Alcyone...

06:49.440 --> 06:51.570
Lady Philomela...

06:52.240 --> 06:55.710
I must be leaving now.

06:56.540 --> 06:58.220
Why did you...

06:59.090 --> 07:02.230
You weren't like this before.

07:02.900 --> 07:06.260
But now, you...

07:06.820 --> 07:13.280
I remembered that I was created for you.

07:14.100 --> 07:17.910
You were supposed to be my purpose.

07:18.710 --> 07:21.510
And yet, I could not protect you.

07:25.810 --> 07:30.460
I apologize for my failure.

07:31.080 --> 07:32.390
No!

07:32.950 --> 07:33.790
No—

07:33.260 --> 07:38.210
Please have my memories as reparation.

07:39.760 --> 07:44.050
Lady Iris had instructed me to keep records.

07:45.030 --> 07:49.470
Although I don't know the difference 
between a record and a memory,

07:49.850 --> 07:54.490
I hope it is of use to you.

07:54.840 --> 07:55.940
Alcyone—

08:18.730 --> 08:25.300
Now, even without me here, 
you'll be all right.

08:39.040 --> 08:41.120
But since they're your records...

08:41.840 --> 08:44.210
You're not in them...

08:58.040 --> 09:00.050
Father?

09:00.360 --> 09:02.640
Is it you, Adam?

09:03.030 --> 09:05.110
Philomela's father?

09:05.110 --> 09:06.700
I thought you were dead.

09:07.540 --> 09:10.450
I'm me, and not Adam.

09:11.460 --> 09:14.110
Adam was really hoping it wouldn't be you.

09:14.660 --> 09:20.740
That you wouldn't be the one to destroy 
your granddaughter's guardian.

09:21.520 --> 09:24.320
But it all turned out as he'd predicted.

09:24.590 --> 09:27.190
I have no need of you if you aren't him!

09:30.820 --> 09:34.630
I'm a curse. A facsimile of 
Adam's memories and shape.

09:34.990 --> 09:37.550
The shadow of the deceased, 
imbued with memories.

09:37.550 --> 09:39.150
You could say I'm a program.

09:39.900 --> 09:41.890
That won't reach me.

09:42.460 --> 09:45.140
But I can reach <i>you</i>.

09:46.500 --> 09:49.480
You, Lizbeth Sargant.

09:54.350 --> 09:56.120
What is this?

09:56.460 --> 09:58.820
Adam's final act of spite.

09:59.220 --> 10:04.920
Adam snuck a curse within Alcyone 
that would retaliate against

10:04.920 --> 10:07.400
whoever destroyed her 
and threatened Philomela.

10:08.140 --> 10:09.040
In other words...

10:10.830 --> 10:13.330
My duty is to destroy you.

10:15.940 --> 10:17.170
Hold it.

10:17.170 --> 10:18.520
Lucy!

10:18.520 --> 10:21.480
She still has a lot she needs to tell me.

10:21.960 --> 10:24.800
Would this not satisfy your 
need for revenge as well?

10:25.380 --> 10:28.300
If I wanted her dead,
I would kill her myself.

10:28.640 --> 10:31.740
But I haven't even had a chance 
to hear an explanation.

10:31.740 --> 10:36.570
I won't stand for her dying just 
so she can get off the hook.

10:37.940 --> 10:39.420
She's mine. You can't have her.

10:41.610 --> 10:44.370
What an unusually 
straightforward girl for your time.

10:44.850 --> 10:47.500
You've made good friends, Philomela.

10:47.500 --> 10:48.740
F-Friends?!

10:49.790 --> 10:51.670
Father...

10:51.670 --> 10:53.120
I won't hand her to you, though.

10:53.590 --> 10:56.650
Your hatred is irrelevant to Adam.

10:57.190 --> 10:59.640
I'm made of Adam's hatred.

10:59.640 --> 11:01.880
She's certainly not yours.

11:10.100 --> 11:11.980
The shouting...

11:16.160 --> 11:17.570
Don't touch that!

11:17.570 --> 11:19.830
It'll take more than just your magic power.

11:27.930 --> 11:28.520
Give—

11:28.520 --> 11:29.120
Give her back!

11:29.800 --> 11:33.010
That woman is my prey!

11:42.410 --> 11:50.620
If a parent's duty is to love and to hold 
dear, so too is it to tease the child.

11:51.710 --> 11:55.140
Is it also, then, the child's 
duty to drag down the parent?

11:59.320 --> 12:04.480
Bitch of the wastelands. 
A heroic, vile mother.

12:04.480 --> 12:06.230
A splendid display of reckless valor.

12:07.120 --> 12:09.950
You have my gratitude, 
god howling in the twilight.

12:13.890 --> 12:16.930
Goddess... Morrígan.

12:23.330 --> 12:25.050
Why are you here?

12:25.430 --> 12:28.970
The war hasn't ended yet, has it?

12:28.970 --> 12:34.760
Should there be a mother and son steeping 
their souls in revenge of days long past,

12:34.760 --> 12:38.550
that land is mine to have and mine to rule.

12:42.040 --> 12:44.390
I see you've crawled out of your roost.

12:44.390 --> 12:46.160
Such arrogance.

12:46.630 --> 12:52.540
You, who defiles my grounds, foreign 
god drifting between time and place...

12:53.160 --> 12:55.420
This here is my territory.

12:55.420 --> 12:57.160
My shores.

12:57.160 --> 13:00.350
I bring you a prophecy of doom.

13:01.010 --> 13:03.070
Well, it's decided to show up.

13:03.070 --> 13:04.710
Elias, what is that?

13:04.710 --> 13:08.470
What you would call a god, in a sense.

13:08.470 --> 13:09.740
This?

13:09.740 --> 13:10.970
A god?

13:11.470 --> 13:13.740
Not a complete one, though.

13:13.740 --> 13:17.550
It hasn't been given a name 
the way Morrígan has.

13:17.550 --> 13:20.950
It must have come out from 
having swallowed that woman.

13:21.410 --> 13:22.990
What a fool.

13:31.300 --> 13:33.920
You, hex who exists for just one man...

13:34.280 --> 13:38.430
Your duty has yet to be 
fulfilled, you must be aware.

13:39.220 --> 13:41.010
Yes, that's right.

13:41.010 --> 13:42.120
You're correct.

13:42.430 --> 13:44.840
Then become my claw.

13:45.790 --> 13:49.960
Become the accursed spear 
that slaughters that beast.

13:55.940 --> 13:57.440
Fath—

13:58.670 --> 14:02.750
You shouldn't use such a word for me.

14:06.490 --> 14:10.550
To think I have two opportunities to 
swing my spear in just one festival...

14:11.070 --> 14:13.240
'Tis a good day!

14:14.100 --> 14:16.220
My maiden...

14:17.750 --> 14:23.910
Though I was given a name, 
I am now but a forgotten shadow.

14:23.910 --> 14:27.920
I cannot myself be their end.

14:38.650 --> 14:43.870
With so many branches, it wouldn't be 
strategic to call upon my soldiers.

14:46.070 --> 14:48.610
Not as easy as that boy, is it?

14:53.000 --> 14:54.120
Hey!

14:54.120 --> 14:55.780
You guys need a hand, don't you?

14:57.960 --> 15:01.060
Chise, why are you grinning?

15:02.950 --> 15:05.980
She must be under the 
influence of the goddess.

15:05.980 --> 15:09.550
I was in need of a hunting 
dog to chase down the game.

15:11.490 --> 15:15.190
Clever dog, jump and bark 
to your heart's content.

15:15.190 --> 15:16.550
That's it?

15:16.550 --> 15:19.780
Distract it and earn some time.

15:40.190 --> 15:43.150
Is she going to deal with it?

15:43.150 --> 15:44.280
I don't know.

15:44.280 --> 15:45.350
But...

15:45.350 --> 15:48.460
It doesn't look like she's trying to end it.

15:48.460 --> 15:50.230
After all that bluster?

15:50.540 --> 15:52.470
It's absorbing magic power.

15:53.590 --> 15:56.220
It might be dangerous, even for a deity.

16:00.250 --> 16:01.450
It noticed us!

16:03.990 --> 16:05.140
Isaac!

16:05.510 --> 16:06.580
Philomela!

16:14.910 --> 16:16.420
Philomela, are you all right?

16:18.960 --> 16:20.030
Lucy!

16:24.220 --> 16:25.670
Get inside me!

16:28.500 --> 16:30.120
Let me go, damn it!

16:30.120 --> 16:30.770
No.

16:30.770 --> 16:33.320
Touch it, and this happens.

16:33.320 --> 16:34.300
Stay here.

16:35.180 --> 16:37.020
Do you think you're making things right?

16:38.920 --> 16:41.440
You're a mere child.

16:41.440 --> 16:43.180
Children must live.

16:43.830 --> 16:46.190
You seem lucid right now.

16:46.190 --> 16:47.040
Don't talk!

16:47.040 --> 16:48.130
You'll bite your tongue!

16:49.640 --> 16:51.910
Why did you attack my home?

16:52.410 --> 16:53.410
I don't know.

16:53.980 --> 16:57.240
But it must have something 
to do with that book.

16:57.240 --> 17:00.710
Before she was ordered to make the kill,

17:00.710 --> 17:04.160
that woman handed the book to 
a man who reeked of spiders.

17:04.990 --> 17:08.430
<i>Do you mean she was our client?!</i>

17:08.430 --> 17:09.550
Not again!

17:10.450 --> 17:12.080
Hold on to me!

17:16.680 --> 17:19.260
There's no end in sight.

17:19.260 --> 17:21.510
What is the goddess doing, playing around?

17:22.970 --> 17:27.620
Though I was given a name, 
I am now but a forgotten shadow.

17:27.620 --> 17:31.410
I cannot myself be their end.

17:31.780 --> 17:36.740
Maybe we have to be the ones to end it.

17:36.740 --> 17:39.120
We do?

17:39.350 --> 17:40.870
I see.

17:40.870 --> 17:46.180
If it was a human that summoned that thing, 
it has to be a human that sends it away.

17:46.740 --> 17:48.440
But how?

17:48.910 --> 17:51.790
It was summoned through the magic book.

17:51.790 --> 17:54.060
So we should probably use the magic book.

17:54.060 --> 17:55.740
That should be right.

17:55.740 --> 17:58.540
Where's the book right now, then?

17:59.280 --> 18:00.210
In there.

18:01.060 --> 18:03.760
Swallowed along with my grandmother.

18:04.470 --> 18:10.180
Chise, nothing happened 
to me when it touched me.

18:10.930 --> 18:15.730
I must still be recognized 
as the book's user.

18:16.350 --> 18:21.800
So I might be able to get the book back.

18:21.800 --> 18:22.570
That's—

18:23.790 --> 18:26.100
Absolutely not!

18:26.490 --> 18:28.770
L-Lucy. Isaac.

18:28.770 --> 18:29.970
You were listening?

18:30.880 --> 18:33.430
She's distracting it right now.

18:34.710 --> 18:37.140
Look at your flimsy limbs.

18:37.140 --> 18:39.780
It might not absorb your 
magic power, but at best,

18:39.780 --> 18:41.540
it'll knock you around or impale you.

18:41.960 --> 18:43.240
You're a moron.

18:43.820 --> 18:44.770
But...

18:45.000 --> 18:48.280
We just need that magic book back, right?

18:48.750 --> 18:53.080
Listen, you're the only one here 
who can deal with that book.

18:54.530 --> 18:59.790
Our top priority is to get that 
book back without losing you.

19:01.120 --> 19:02.730
I agree with that.

19:03.510 --> 19:06.530
Philomela, is there anything else you need?

19:07.130 --> 19:10.030
I need magic power to control it.

19:10.760 --> 19:12.620
Use me, then.

19:13.280 --> 19:14.500
What?

19:16.430 --> 19:18.340
Chise, you...

19:19.050 --> 19:22.360
This is the best course of action.

19:22.360 --> 19:24.220
It's my own decision.

19:24.220 --> 19:27.380
In that case, you can use mine, too.

19:29.610 --> 19:32.810
As long as you aren't just taking 
it from me without telling me.

19:32.810 --> 19:35.190
But how do we reach the book?

19:35.590 --> 19:39.120
Distracting it seems to work.

19:39.120 --> 19:41.650
Not with our legs, though.

19:41.650 --> 19:43.270
We'll be mummies in no time.

19:46.410 --> 19:47.530
What?

19:48.520 --> 19:50.340
Goddess, there's no end to this!

19:50.340 --> 19:53.410
I'm growing bored of dancing.

19:53.900 --> 19:56.620
I thought the human children might move...

19:56.620 --> 19:58.060
But we're out of time.

20:03.450 --> 20:07.880
You really aren't shy about making 
demands of me anymore, Chise.

20:08.860 --> 20:11.410
There's a phrase in Japanese that means,

20:11.410 --> 20:14.270
"Even if it's your parents who are 
standing around, put them to work."

20:14.270 --> 20:15.700
Sheesh.

20:17.890 --> 20:19.260
This way!

20:22.010 --> 20:25.190
Philomela, do you know where that book is?

20:30.620 --> 20:33.320
Inside the big eyeball!

20:36.550 --> 20:39.180
King of the east, hauling the storms...

20:39.180 --> 20:43.410
By your hands, deafen the tyrants.

20:43.650 --> 20:47.440
By your crown, blind the eyes of the vile.

20:48.580 --> 20:53.920
By your breath, send beyond 
the fog your raised child.

21:01.010 --> 21:02.200
Here!

21:02.200 --> 21:05.990
Morrígan, attack it with your spear here!

21:06.740 --> 21:12.200
I haven't the heart to deny a 
young child such an ardent wish.

21:12.670 --> 21:16.080
You, who walk through the 
discarded carcasses of time...

21:16.590 --> 21:19.680
Time to know the taste of the curse!

22:05.720 --> 22:06.920
Magic power...
